# 1Password secret reference for Argus.
#
#   cp op.env.example op.env
#
# `./run.sh up` detects this file and resolves the reference with
# `op run`, injecting the token directly into the container's
# environment. The token never lands on disk, never enters the image,
# and never appears in your shell history.
#
# This file is safe to copy; op.env is gitignored, and even that holds
# only a reference, never a token.
#
# Do not have 1Password? Skip this entirely - run.sh falls back to your
# `gh auth login`. See the README for both paths.

# Format: op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
ARGUS_GITHUB_TOKEN=op://Private/GitHub Argus Token/credential

# IMPORTANT: use YOUR OWN token in YOUR OWN private vault.
#
# Argus scopes everything to whoever the token belongs to - your review
# requests, your teams, your branches. Pointing several people at one
# shared item would show them all the same person's dashboard, which
# defeats the point.
